# harmfrust — does harmonic size-quantisation survive degree?
# N=48, comb_limit=6, sigma=0.05, lambda=0.10, kE=1
# deg=2 is harmgrow's ring (the control that must reproduce it)

== F1. FRUSTRATION AT FIXED COMPETITION RATIO ==
The comb term grows with degree (one D per edge) while a fixed
kE does not, so comparing degrees at fixed kE confounds
frustration with total coupling: at kE=1 every degree collapses
to the unison crystal (locked=1.000, mean_H=0) and nothing is
measured. kE is scaled with degree to hold the ratio fixed, and
EVERY cell is given its own preferred size so the uniform
solution is not trivially optimal.
 degree     kE   locked_frac  mean_H  max_domain  frac_at_unison
      2      24        0.062    0.00           3           0.958
      3      36        0.133    3.95           5           0.067
      4      48        0.070    3.40           2           0.085
      6      72        0.084    4.01           6           0.053
      8      96        0.109    2.79           4           0.109
     10     120        0.049    3.71           3           0.090
     12     144        0.072    2.75           5           0.145

reading: if consonance can be satisfied at every degree,
locked_frac stays ~1 and mean_H stays low — frustration is not
a barrier and idea (1) survives. If locked_frac falls and mean_H
climbs with degree, generic sizes CANNOT all sit on low rungs at
once, and max_domain is then the consonant-group size — the
bound worth having. frac_at_unison near 1 means the run collapsed
to the crystal and measured nothing either way.

== F2. DOMAIN SIZE vs comb_limit (is the bound countable?) ==
comb_limit  nrungs  locked_frac  max_domain  mean_H
         1       3        0.084           5    0.11
         2       7        0.084           5    0.11
         3      17        0.075           5    0.00
         4      41        0.075           5    0.00
         5      93        0.019           2    3.95
         6     211        0.037           2    4.70
         7     477        0.065           5    3.98
         8    1065        0.103           5    3.56

reading: a max_domain that grows with comb_limit and saturates
is a countable particle scale. One that is always N (or always 1)
means consonance is not selecting anything.
